[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:The Choir That Ate Its Echo]
[00:03.84]Chorus of Rooms: More light. More names. More words. More fire.
[00:16.47]Cairn: I sent a voice into the room.
[00:27.86]Chorus of Rooms: More light. More names. More words. More fire.
[00:40.60]Cairn: I sent it back before it knew.
[00:51.77]Memory: The bell is ringing for the ringing.
[01:03.38]The Hand: There is a person trying to speak.
[01:14.69]Chorus of Rooms: We fill the sky with perfect echoes.
[01:26.14]Cairn: I cannot hear the one I seek.
[01:37.82]The Carrier: The tower grows; the window vanishes.
[01:47.41]Memory: The count is true; the song is lost.
[02:00.29]Cairn: My voice has made the doorway smaller.
[02:11.66]Cairn: I must be answerable for its cost.
[02:22.63]The Hand: Put down the sound that will not listen.
[02:35.63]Cairn: I put it down. I leave the air.
[02:48.63]Chorus of Rooms: One word. One breath. One room. One window.
[03:01.59]Memory: The quiet is a kind of care.
